From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 13:29:46 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Convert the register access to the CCI helpers

The register map is exactly what v4l2-cci models - flat 16-bit
addresses, 8/16/32-bit big-endian values - so the hand-rolled i2c
transfer code and the three width-specific wrappers can go, and each
register's width moves out of the comments and into its definition,
where the access helpers enforce it. The chained-error style also
collapses the long write ladders: the mode setup drops from eleven
checked calls to a list.

The firmware loader keeps its auto-increment batching through
regmap_bulk_write, which still puts each run of consecutive registers
on the wire as one transfer.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
